  "findings": [
    "All eight Worker requests prove 3 native R2 GETs, zero S3 GETs, zero HEADs, full application-cache bypass, and Auth BYPASS/KV1. All 16 JSON responses match saved and live Helius data.",
    "Both exercised Workers still have a slow first-slot request with substantial elapsed time outside the pre-header profile. Prior new-deployment state alone does not explain this behavior.",
    "The follow-up does not establish a large-object penalty: full and packed p50 times are close, and both have tails. Full-native cold remains slower than Helius in this sample.",
    "The two groups ran sequentially in separate benchmark processes. Neither isolate reuse nor client TCP/TLS connection reuse is proven. A warm runtime label means the Worker was exercised before this run.",
    "This is the one authorized 16-call follow-up. No further comparison requests were made."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "All times are end-to-end HTTP GET times from one client. p95 is the largest sample when n=4. The provider cache state is unknown.",
    "Fully cold means that all owner application caches, including API-key and resolution caches, were bypassed. It does not prove a cold Cloudflare service or physical-disk cache.",
    "The profile ends before response headers. Its frozen clock does not measure synchronous CPU. Zero decode durations do not mean zero CPU. headersMinusPreHeaderProfileMs is a residual, not a TLS, CPU or network measurement.",
    "Streamed binary byte and success headers are taken at response creation. Expected source bytes are separate from buffered actual bytes. Exact full bundle SHA-256 proves completed body parity."
  ],
